## Admin pages
Both live under `apps/web/src/app/(dashboard)/admin/` behind an admin-only server gate (`layout.tsx` redirects non-admins):

- `users/` — user management backed by the `users` tRPC router (`packages/api/src/router/users.ts`, all `adminProcedure`). `users/page.tsx` titles the page and renders `users.client.tsx`, which lists accounts in the shuip `DataTableShell` (search + sort + pages, all on the server: see [Data layer](data-layer.md)) with a **Create user** dialog that calls `users.create` — the server generates a random password and returns it once. `users/[id]/page.tsx` titles the page and renders `user.client.tsx`, a per-user editor: display name / first / last / phone are **inline-edit** fields (`users.update`), alongside role (`users.setRole`, a select of the roles of the database, absent on your own account), password reset (`users.setPassword`, shown once), ban/unban (`users.setBanned`) and delete (`users.remove`). The router calls the Better Auth admin API per-request (`createAuth(ctx.db).api.*` with `ctx.headers`) for anything touching credentials or sessions, and writes profile columns directly via Drizzle.
- `roles/page.tsx` — **Roles**: the role × permission matrix, editable (see "Editing roles"). `page.tsx` guards with `requireAdmin`, prefetches `roles.matrix` and renders `roles.client.tsx`: a **New role** dialog (`create-role-dialog.tsx`) and `role-matrix.tsx`. The `admin` column is the compiled grants (`ADMIN_PERMISSIONS`) and the account permissions (`user`, `session`) are shown with no box, because they are never stored; the other columns are the rows of `roles` and `role_permissions`, one labelled box per business permission, and the delete button of a role (absent on `admin` and the default role) opens the confirmation dialog. The table scrolls inside its own container on a phone with the permission names pinned on the left, and the current viewer's column is highlighted.
